863
00:27:42,271 --> 00:27:44,037
more into retirement accounts.

864
00:27:44,388 --> 00:27:45,340
Mistake one.

865
00:27:45,520 --> 00:27:47,412
Stopping during a market drop.

866
00:27:47,592 --> 00:27:49,588
That's when your one hundred dollars buys

867
00:27:49,588 --> 00:27:50,367
the most shares.

868
00:27:50,547 --> 00:27:51,615
Mistake two.

869
00:27:51,795 --> 00:27:53,385
Picking expensive funds.

870
00:27:53,565 --> 00:27:55,581
A high fee on a small balance

871
00:27:55,581 --> 00:27:58,360
still compounds against you for decades.

872
00:27:58,540 --> 00:27:59,574
Mistake three.

873
00:27:59,754 --> 00:28:00,938
Cashing out early.

874
00:28:01,118 --> 00:28:04,455
Withdrawing from retirement accounts early can mean

875
00:28:04,455 --> 00:28:05,763
taxes and penalties,

876
00:28:05,763 --> 00:28:08,119
and it resets the compounding clock.

877
00:28:08,469 --> 00:28:09,490
Mistake four.

878
00:28:09,670 --> 00:28:12,166
Chasing hot tips with your monthly money.

879
00:28:12,346 --> 00:28:14,793
Small amounts are easy to gamble with,

880
00:28:14,793 --> 00:28:17,176
and that's exactly why it's tempting.

881
00:28:17,356 --> 00:28:18,970
Keep your core plan boring.

882
00:28:19,150 --> 00:28:20,090
Mistake five.

883
00:28:20,270 --> 00:28:21,733
Never increasing the amount.

884
00:28:21,913 --> 00:28:24,022
One hundred dollars is a wonderful start,

885
00:28:24,022 --> 00:28:25,566
but the people who end up with

886
00:28:25,566 --> 00:28:27,160
the most are the ones who raise

887
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:28,241
it whenever they can.

888
00:28:28,591 --> 00:28:30,884
So what can roughly fifty two thousand

889
00:28:30,884 --> 00:28:33,116
dollars actually do for you in twenty

890
00:28:33,116 --> 00:28:33,478
years?

891
00:28:33,658 --> 00:28:34,552
Option one.

892
00:28:34,732 --> 00:28:36,380
It can be the backbone of your

893
00:28:36,380 --> 00:28:36,985
safety net.

894
00:28:37,165 --> 00:28:38,894
With that much invested,

895
00:28:38,894 --> 00:28:40,911
a job loss or a medical bill

896
00:28:40,911 --> 00:28:42,207
becomes a setback,

897
00:28:42,207 --> 00:28:43,144
not a crisis.

898
00:28:43,324 --> 00:28:45,606
That kind of security changes how you

899
00:28:45,606 --> 00:28:46,716
negotiate at work,

900
00:28:46,716 --> 00:28:48,134
how you sleep at night,

901
00:28:48,134 --> 00:28:49,984
and how much risk you can take

902
00:28:49,984 --> 00:28:51,033
with your career.

903
00:28:51,383 --> 00:28:52,427
Option two.

904
00:28:52,607 --> 00:28:53,734
It can keep growing.

905
00:28:53,914 --> 00:28:56,282
If you stop contributing at year twenty

906
00:28:56,282 --> 00:28:58,651
and simply leave the fifty two thousand

907
00:28:58,651 --> 00:29:01,202
invested at the same seven percent average

908
00:29:01,202 --> 00:29:03,632
return, it could roughly double again in

909
00:29:03,632 --> 00:29:04,604
about ten years,

910
00:29:04,604 --> 00:29:06,243
by the rule of seventy two.

911
00:29:06,423 --> 00:29:08,449
Your one hundred dollars a month keeps

912
00:29:08,449 --> 00:29:10,475
working long after you stop paying in.

913
00:29:10,826 --> 00:29:11,789
Option three.

914
00:29:11,969 --> 00:29:13,479
It can produce income.

915
00:29:13,659 --> 00:29:16,509
Using the four percent guideline many retirement

916
00:29:16,509 --> 00:29:19,479
planners mention, fifty two thousand dollars could

917
00:29:19,479 --> 00:29:22,508
support roughly two thousand dollars of withdrawals

918
00:29:22,508 --> 00:29:22,923
a year.

919
00:29:23,103 --> 00:29:24,600
That's not a full income,

920
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:26,576
but it's a meaningful supplement,

921
00:29:26,576 --> 00:29:28,611
and it came from money most people

922
00:29:28,611 --> 00:29:29,988
never noticed spending.

923
00:29:30,338 --> 00:29:31,419
And option four,

924
00:29:31,419 --> 00:29:32,973
the most important one.

925
00:29:33,153 --> 00:29:34,567
It can prove to you that this

926
00:29:34,567 --> 00:29:34,860
works.

927
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:37,359
Once you've watched one hundred dollars a

928
00:29:37,359 --> 00:29:39,283
month turn into tens of thousands,

929
00:29:39,283 --> 00:29:41,320
you'll never look at small money the

930
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:42,168
same way again.

931
00:29:42,348 --> 00:29:44,525
That belief is often worth more than

932
00:29:44,525 --> 00:29:45,553
the money itself.

933
00:29:45,903 --> 00:29:47,369
Let me show you how this plays

934
00:29:47,369 --> 00:29:48,445
out with three people.

935
00:29:48,796 --> 00:29:51,530
Alex starts investing one hundred dollars a

936
00:29:51,530 --> 00:29:54,073
month at twenty five and never increases

937
00:29:54,073 --> 00:29:54,264
it.

938
00:29:54,444 --> 00:29:55,341
At sixty five,

939
00:29:55,341 --> 00:29:57,967
at a seven percent average yearly return,

940
00:29:57,967 --> 00:30:00,401
that could grow to roughly two hundred

941
00:30:00,401 --> 00:30:01,874
sixty thousand dollars.

942
00:30:02,054 --> 00:30:03,992
Not bad for money that felt too

943
00:30:03,992 --> 00:30:04,992
small to matter.

944
00:30:05,342 --> 00:30:07,876
Jamie waits until thirty five to start,

945
00:30:07,876 --> 00:30:10,345
also with one hundred dollars a month.

946
00:30:10,525 --> 00:30:11,297
At sixty five,

947
00:30:11,297 --> 00:30:13,501
that could be roughly one hundred twenty

948
00:30:13,501 --> 00:30:14,659
two thousand dollars.

949
00:30:14,839 --> 00:30:17,057
Waiting ten years cut the result by

950
00:30:17,057 --> 00:30:18,008
more than half.

951
00:30:18,358 --> 00:30:20,614
Morgan starts at twenty five with one

952
00:30:20,614 --> 00:30:22,077
hundred dollars a month,

953
00:30:22,077 --> 00:30:24,821
and increases the contribution a little every

954
00:30:24,821 --> 00:30:25,126
year.

955
00:30:25,306 --> 00:30:25,947
By the end,

956
00:30:25,947 --> 00:30:28,044
Morgan could have far more than both

957
00:30:28,044 --> 00:30:28,511
of them.

958
00:30:28,691 --> 00:30:30,014
Same starting amount.

959
00:30:30,194 --> 00:30:32,455
The difference was starting early and growing

960
00:30:32,455 --> 00:30:32,957
the habit.

961
00:30:33,308 --> 00:30:34,144
Question one.

962
00:30:34,324 --> 00:30:36,257
Is one hundred dollars a month really

963
00:30:36,257 --> 00:30:36,727
worth it?

964
00:30:36,907 --> 00:30:37,394
Yes.

965
00:30:37,574 --> 00:30:39,031
It builds the habit,

966
00:30:39,031 --> 00:30:42,016
gets compounding started and grows into a

967
00:30:42,016 --> 00:30:44,273
meaningful amount over decades.

968
00:30:44,453 --> 00:30:46,366
And it usually becomes more than one

969
00:30:46,366 --> 00:30:48,331
hundred dollars as your income grows.

970
00:30:48,681 --> 00:30:49,528
Question two.

971
00:30:49,708 --> 00:30:51,674
What if I can only invest fifty

972
00:30:51,674 --> 00:30:52,181
dollars?

973
00:30:52,361 --> 00:30:53,510
Start with fifty.

974
00:30:53,690 --> 00:30:57,123
Many brokerages allow small amounts and fractional

975
00:30:57,123 --> 00:30:57,603
shares.

976
00:30:57,783 --> 00:30:59,826
The habit matters more than the amount.

977
00:31:00,177 --> 00:31:01,303
Question three.

978
00:31:01,483 --> 00:31:03,689
What if the market crashes right after

979
00:31:03,689 --> 00:31:04,153
I start?

980
00:31:04,333 --> 00:31:06,237
Then you're buying at lower prices.

981
00:31:06,417 --> 00:31:07,820
For a twenty year plan,

982
00:31:07,820 --> 00:31:09,649
early drops can actually help,

983
00:31:09,649 --> 00:31:11,479
as long as you keep investing.

984
00:31:11,829 --> 00:31:12,757
Question four.

985
00:31:12,937 --> 00:31:14,848
Should I invest or pay off my

986
00:31:14,848 --> 00:31:15,770
student loans?

987
00:31:15,950 --> 00:31:17,854
It depends on the interest rate.

988
00:31:18,034 --> 00:31:20,438
High interest debt usually comes first.

989
00:31:20,618 --> 00:31:22,081
For low interest debt,

990
00:31:22,081 --> 00:31:23,412
many people do both,

991
00:31:23,412 --> 00:31:25,807
especially to get an employer match.

992
00:31:26,158 --> 00:31:27,214
Question five.

993
00:31:27,394 --> 00:31:29,606
Should I invest my one hundred dollars

994
00:31:29,606 --> 00:31:30,887
all at once each year,

995
00:31:30,887 --> 00:31:31,527
or monthly?

996
00:31:31,707 --> 00:31:34,633
Research on lump sum versus monthly investing

997
00:31:34,633 --> 00:31:38,014
suggests that investing sooner has historically done

998
00:31:38,014 --> 00:31:39,184
better more often,

999
00:31:39,184 --> 00:31:41,785
because markets have tended to rise over

1000
00:31:41,785 --> 00:31:42,110
time.

1001
00:31:42,290 --> 00:31:43,510
But for most people,

1002
00:31:43,510 --> 00:31:46,012
money arrives monthly with each paycheck,

1003
00:31:46,012 --> 00:31:48,393
so investing monthly is the natural and

1004
00:31:48,393 --> 00:31:49,430
practical choice.

1005
00:31:49,610 --> 00:31:51,833
The important thing is that it happens

1006
00:31:51,833 --> 00:31:52,594
consistently.

1007
00:31:52,944 --> 00:31:54,105
Question six.

1008
00:31:54,285 --> 00:31:55,597
Can I lose all my money?

1009
00:31:55,777 --> 00:31:57,365
With a single stock,

1010
00:31:57,365 --> 00:31:59,271
yes, a company can fail.

1011
00:31:59,451 --> 00:32:01,897
With a broad index fund holding hundreds

1012
00:32:01,897 --> 00:32:03,487
or thousands of companies,

1013
00:32:03,487 --> 00:32:06,484
losing everything would require nearly the entire

1014
00:32:06,484 --> 00:32:08,379
market to collapse permanently.

1015
00:32:08,559 --> 00:32:10,824
Values can still drop sharply for a

1016
00:32:10,824 --> 00:32:12,959
time, which is why money you need

1017
00:32:12,959 --> 00:32:14,771
soon shouldn't be in stocks.

1018
00:32:15,121 --> 00:32:15,933
Quick recap.

1019
00:32:16,113 --> 00:32:17,832
Angle one, the numbers.

1020
00:32:18,012 --> 00:32:19,969
Time is the main ingredient,

1021
00:32:19,969 --> 00:32:21,926
the rate changes everything,

1022
00:32:21,926 --> 00:32:23,044
fees eat growth,

1023
00:32:23,044 --> 00:32:25,071
inflation shrinks the number,

1024
00:32:25,071 --> 00:32:26,889
the right account matters,

1025
00:32:26,889 --> 00:32:29,545
raising the amount changes everything,

1026
00:32:29,545 --> 00:32:31,572
and bad years are part of it.

1027
00:32:31,922 --> 00:32:34,058
Angle two, the psychology.

1028
00:32:34,238 --> 00:32:35,736
It feels too small,

1029
00:32:35,736 --> 00:32:37,628
there's no perfect time,

1030
00:32:37,628 --> 00:32:40,229
present bias, checking too often,

1031
00:32:40,229 --> 00:32:42,279
comparing, fear of losing,

1032
00:32:42,279 --> 00:32:44,013
and fading motivation.

1033
00:32:44,364 --> 00:32:46,001
Angle three, the playbook.

1034
00:32:46,181 --> 00:32:49,213
Emergency fund, high interest debt,

1035
00:32:49,213 --> 00:32:51,379
employer match, Roth IRA,

1036
00:32:51,379 --> 00:32:53,286
simple low cost funds,

1037
00:32:53,286 --> 00:32:55,538
and automate and increase.

1038
00:32:55,889 --> 00:32:57,838
One hundred dollars a month won't change

1039
00:32:57,838 --> 00:32:58,861
your life this month.

1040
00:32:59,041 --> 00:33:00,202
But in twenty years,

1041
00:33:00,202 --> 00:33:01,653
it can change everything.

1042
00:33:01,833 --> 00:33:02,785
Set it up today.

1043
00:33:02,965 --> 00:33:04,382
If you want the full plan,

1044
00:33:04,382 --> 00:33:05,472
it's in my playbook,

1045
00:33:05,472 --> 00:33:06,889
linked in the description.

1046
00:33:07,069 --> 00:33:08,757
Tell me in the comments how many

1047
00:33:08,757 --> 00:33:10,076
years you have to invest.

1048
00:33:10,256 --> 00:33:11,510
I'm Ryan Rover.

1049
00:33:11,690 --> 00:33:12,909
See you in the next one.
